warnings or errors.\n- **Integration tests:** all six new `HomePageTest` tests pass.\n- **Browser test:** `TheHomePageSaysWhatTheShopSells` failed at first. The stylesheet renders the subtitle in capitals, and the test read the text as displayed (\"BOOKS, MODELLING …\"). I changed the two page-object methods this stage had added (`SubtitleAsync` and `DescriptionAsync` in `tests/DcaShop.E2eTests/Pages/HomePage.cs`) to read the paragraph's wording instead of its display casing. The test's assertions are unchanged, and it now passes.\n- **Formatting:** `dotnet format` has run and the format check is clean.\n\n**Not checked:** the seven break patches. Applying them to `Index.cshtml` (even a dry-run `git apply --check`) needed approval I didn't have, so the gate's scratch-copy run will be the first time they're tested.\n\n`tasks/CAT-04/tests.md` now records all of this. The test-to-scenario table and the break files are unchanged.","ttft_ms":2342,"type":"result","duration_ms":131365,"uuid":"40fb02e2-b966-455f-9e89-efb17b7836e5","ttft_stream_ms":1798,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1798,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
